    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__micro-os-plus-diag-trace-c-api-implementation_1gac34c391936f919c141bc38ec5b5a1db9" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void micro_os_plus_trace_flush</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>micro_os_plus_trace_flush</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Flush the trace output channel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Parameters</title><para>None. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Returns</title><para>Nothing.</para>
</simplesect>
For buffered output channels, this function must drain any internally buffered data to the output device. For unbuffered or character-mode channels (e.g. ITM), the body can be left empty. No assumptions are made about thread safety or re-entrancy; the caller is responsible for ensuring that concurrent calls do not occur. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
