        <definition>void micro_os_plus_trace_initialise</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>micro_os_plus_trace_initialise</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Initialise the trace output channel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Parameters</title><para>None. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Returns</title><para>Nothing.</para>
</simplesect>
This function is called during startup, as early as possible, to enable the trace channel. The user must provide a definition of this function that configures the underlying output device (e.g. a semihosting channel, or an ITM port). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
